      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T16:52:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Keith reported that PD_LPM_DEBOUNCE_US set to 10ms doesn\u0027t work with TUSB422 (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2606235).\nCurrent debounce delay (100ms) breaks octopus boards eg. bobba.\n\nIn https://issuetracker.google.com/176986511#comment6 I described what happens when soft reset is performed while waking from Low Power Mode. In one sentence, we are losing DRP result and device always sets CC lines to Rd. TUSB422 and RT1715 was working only because PD_LPM_DEBOUNCE_US was long enough (longer than tDRP).\n\nI\u0027m a bit surprised that no one discovered it.\n\nTUSB422 documentation (https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tusb422.pdf) page 42 mentions that TCPC will accept I2CIdle command but will do nothing with it. Also searched for information about Low Power Mode or wake and found nothing. I have doubts whether Low Power Mode is implemented in this TCPC.",
